1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,100
Messi Bids Farewell to the World Stage.

2
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:14,225
Lionel Messi's extraordinary World Cup journey came to an end at the 2026 tournament, where the 39-year-old icon recorded 8 goals and 4 assists across the competition.

3
00:00:14,225 --> 00:00:26,175
Argentina's run to the final fell just short against Spain, but Messi's individual brilliance throughout the group stage and knockout rounds reminded the world why he is considered one of the greatest players in history.

4
00:00:26,175 --> 00:00:37,800
His eight goals moved him into second place on the all-time World Cup scoring list behind Miroslav Klose, while his four assists gave him a hand in 12 of Argentina's 16 goals in the tournament.

5
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:46,187
The final whistle at MetLife Stadium triggered an emotional farewell as teammates and opponents alike sought to embrace the seven-time Ballon d'Or winner.

6
00:00:46,187 --> 00:00:52,987
FIFA President Gianni Infantino called Messi's World Cup career "unmatched in its brilliance and longevity.

7
00:00:52,987 --> 00:01:06,162
The tournament's expanded 48-team format gave Messi additional matches to showcase his talents, and he delivered consistently, leaving the global game with a lasting memory of his final bow on football's grandest stage.

